nal environment deteriorates further for Republicans or early state polling shows a competitive race, the margin could narrow meaningfully.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Tennessee remains one of the more reliably Republican states in presidential elections, and the fundamentals point the same way: a partisan lean of roughly fourteen points toward the GOP and recent double-digit Republican margins at the top of the ticket. With the incumbent term-limited, both parties face open contests, and no general-election polls in the state are available yet.\n\nThe main caution flag for Republicans is the president's standing: approval has slipped below fifty percent in Tennessee, and coverage describes it as underwater. That suggests a somewhat less friendly environment than in recent cycles, but state partisanship in presidential races has proven durable. The forecast expects the Republican nominee to carry the state by a comfortable double-digit margin, with enough residual uncertainty to leave a small chance of a closer race if the national climate shifts.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0961, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1038, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1086, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0965, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1008, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0